Firing is handled in the prediction group, next to movement, so the muzzle flash and the recoil kick land on the same tick as the shot:

    if (input.Fire && cooldown <= 0) {
        SpawnMuzzleFlash(ecb, muzzle);
        cooldown = FireRate;
    }

QA on the office machines — all 60 Hz panels — reports nothing. QA on the one 144 Hz machine reports "the gun sometimes fires three flashes per click". You cannot reproduce it, and the shooting logic is obviously correct.

You store the tick a projectile was fired on and expire it after 300 ticks:

    if (currentTick.SerializedData > shot.FiredTick.SerializedData + 300)
        Destroy(projectile);

It is correct. It is tested. It runs in QA for two weeks straight without a single failure, and it runs in the first playtest for about nine hours.
